-- title:
--   A place of the disc centred at each non-varpi prime
-- statement:
--   Fix fields $k_0 \subseteq L \subseteq F$ in a tower, with $L$ of characteristic zero and algebraically closed and $F$ a curve over $L$ (principal divisors exist, every place has residue field finite over $L$, and $\Omega_{F/L}$ is free of rank one over $F$), together with an intermediate field $F_0$ of $F/k_0$ such that $k_0(\mathrm{im}\,L) \sqcup F_0 = F$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $L$, $\bar F$ a field extension of its residue field, and $R$ a regular prolongation of $A$ to $F$ with values in $\bar F$: a valuation subring $R.\mathrm{integers}$ of $F$ with surjective residue map to $\bar F$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal, contracting to $A$ on $L$ and compatible with the residue map of $A$, and such that every nonzero $f \in F$ has an $L$-multiple lying in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ with nonzero residue. Assume given: an intermediate field $K_1$ of $L/k_0$ with $L/K_1$ algebraic, a valuation subring $A_1$ of $K_1$ cut out by $A$, with residue field mapping onto that of $A$; a subring $S_1 \subseteq F$, a ring homomorphism $\varphi_1 : A_1[X] \to S_1$, a homomorphism $\chi_1 : S_1 \to \mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, and a set $D_1$ of places of $F/L$ (valuation subrings of $F$ containing $L$, proper, and principal ideal rings); the compatibilities that $\varphi_1 \circ C$ is the inclusion of $A_1$ into $F$, that $\chi_1 \circ \varphi_1 \circ C$ is the residue map of $A_1$ into the residue field of $A$, and that $\chi_1(\varphi_1 X) = 0$; the description of $D_1$ as the set of places $P$ that are rational (the map $L \to$ residue field of $P$ is onto), for which every $f \in S_1$ is $P$-integral with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f \in A$, and for which $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f$ has $A$-valuation $<1$ exactly when $\chi_1 f = 0$; that $\varphi_1 X$ is not of the form $\varphi_1(C\,c)$; that $S_1$ is a local Noetherian unique factorisation domain whose maximal ideal is $\ker \chi_1$; that $S_1$ lies in $F_1 := k_0(\mathrm{im}\,K_1) \sqcup F_0$ and every element of $F_1$ is a fraction of elements of $S_1$; that any family $c_i \in L$ linearly independent over $K_1$ admits no nontrivial relation $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ with $a_i \in F_1$; that every proper valuation subring of $F$ containing $L$ is a principal ideal ring; a nonzero generator $\varpi$ of the maximal ideal of $A_1$ whose image $\varphi_1(C\,\varpi)$ is prime in $S_1$; the description of $R.\mathrm{integers} \cap F_1$ as the fractions $g/h$ with $g, h \in S_1$ and $\varphi_1(C\,\varpi) \nmid h$; that any section $\chi : S_1 \to A_1$ of $\varphi_1 \circ C$ inducing $\chi_1$ after reduction has kernel generated by $\varphi_1 X - \varphi_1(C\,(\chi(\varphi_1 X)))$; and a branch-integrality hypothesis: for every prime $p$ of $S_1$ not associated to $\varphi_1(C\,\varpi)$ and every $x \in S_1$ there is a monic $r \in A_1[X]$ with $p$ dividing the value at $x$ of $r$ pushed forward along $\varphi_1 \circ C$. Then for every prime $p$ of $S_1$ not associated to $\varphi_1(C\,\varpi)$ there is a place $P \in D_1$ such that, for all $f \in S_1$, $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f = 0$ if and only if $p \mid f$; here $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f$ is the element of $L$ representing the residue class of $f$ at $P$ when $f$ is $P$-integral, and $0$ otherwise.
--
--   This is the branch-place statement of the smooth-point analysis: each prime divisor of the local ring $S_1$ other than the one cutting out the special fibre is the centre of a rational place belonging to the distinguished family $D_1$ of places of the disc. It is used in the proofs that a section through a smooth point determines a unique place of the disc with prescribed values, and in the locality statement for $D_1$ at a smooth point.
